"help.tip.sources"    = "Screenshot mode handles text you <b>cannot select</b> — images, scanned PDFs, video subtitles. Selection mode handles selectable text: no recognition errors and no dragging.<br>To change these combinations: menu bar → <b>Keyboard Shortcuts</b>, click a field and press the new combination.";
"help.tip.level"      = "Without the pin, the window floats on top only at the moment it appears — click any other window and it drops behind, out of your way.";
"help.tip.detection"  = "Language detection: Hangul → Korean, kana → Japanese, Han → Chinese — one character settles it. Only Latin script needs statistical guessing; when it is unsure the language label in the top-left turns <b class=warn>orange with a question mark</b>, and you can switch with <kbd>⌘1</kbd>…<kbd>⌘9</kbd>.";
"help.tip.diagnostics" = "Menu bar → “Permissions & Languages” shows the current state at any time.";
"help.tip.privacy"    = "Browsing data of the built-in window is cleared on quit (currently: <b>%@</b>). This app never records your lookup history, but dictionary sites store “recent searches” in browser storage — hence the default.";

